Diagnosis:
  RendererEngine.close_display_calibration() closed a temporary calibration owner, then restored a differing previous display using replace_display(). That path calls ModernGLPort.initialize_display(), whose blanket _released.clear() erased the still-registered calibration-arena release receipt. A later cleanup therefore had an outstanding catalogue key despite native close having succeeded.

Source diff summary:
  ModernGLPort stores the registration callback as _announce and routes native allocations through announce(key, path). The wrapper forwards registration first, then removes only release receipts for that exact key. initialize_display() no longer clears unrelated receipts. Existing retire_released_resources() remains the explicit post-confirmation clear boundary.
  The owning renderer test covers changed-profile close/restore, retains an unrelated receipt, and verifies failed reallocation of the same key invalidates stale proof and remains outstanding.

